WEBVTT

00:01:35.770 --> 00:01:37.650
You haven't eaten anything at all?

00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:38.440
No...

00:01:39.190 --> 00:01:40.240
Damn it!

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:42.400
I’ll get you something to eat.

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:43.870
Stay here and wait for me.

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:46.870
Nai, don't go <i>anywhere</i>, you understand?

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:33.340
Karoku...

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:43.840
Fortune Cat
Score 2

00:02:45.550 --> 00:02:47.090
About last night's incident,

00:02:47.090 --> 00:02:49.430
Things did not go smoothly, did they?

00:02:49.430 --> 00:02:51.260
Second Ship Captain Hirato.

00:02:51.930 --> 00:02:56.350
Your superior did not seem to provide you with proper discipline.

00:02:56.350 --> 00:02:59.860
It's rude to make such derisive remarks when he's right here...

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:02.230
First Ship Captain, Tsukitachi.

00:03:02.230 --> 00:03:04.370
Do not speak out of turn.

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:08.110
I will reflect on my mistakes and see that it does not happen again.

00:03:08.110 --> 00:03:09.280
Very well.

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:10.870
You are dismissed.

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:15.120
They make such a fuss.

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:18.500
Old men are so stubborn with their stereotypes.

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:20.290
Why did you come with me?

00:03:20.290 --> 00:03:24.010
Well, I thought I might enjoy watching you being reprimanded.

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:27.010
I will shoot you when I see you in the sky.

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:33.520
Moreover, the train jacking was supposed be our mission.

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:35.810
But, you took it over for us.

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:39.690
You owe me one...

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:42.820
Holy, that sounds expensive.

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:46.830
Come, come!

00:03:49.610 --> 00:03:50.580
Here.

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:03.340
And so, after catching all the bad guys in the area,

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:08.130
they will put on a show to apologize for scaring the people.

00:04:08.130 --> 00:04:09.590
A show?

00:04:09.590 --> 00:04:12.350
Yes. A circus show.

00:04:13.430 --> 00:04:14.850
Circus...

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:15.970
That's right.

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:20.020
Karoku.

00:04:20.020 --> 00:04:20.860
Um?

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:25.940
Say, is there a person named Karoku in the Circus?

00:04:25.940 --> 00:04:28.110
Well, I don't know.

00:04:28.110 --> 00:04:30.110
Nana, we're going!

00:04:30.820 --> 00:04:33.000
Sorry. Bye.

00:04:38.290 --> 00:04:39.630
Thank you.

00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:53.140
<i>I've confirmed that boy's location.</i>

00:04:53.800 --> 00:04:55.680
Bring him in right away.

00:04:55.680 --> 00:04:58.730
However, do not injure him.

00:04:58.730 --> 00:04:59.520
<i>Understood.</i>

00:05:08.860 --> 00:05:10.370
That brat!

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:12.620
I'm going to kill him...

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:23.880
H-Hey.

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:24.640
Here.

00:05:27.670 --> 00:05:29.640
Come and see us, okay?

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:31.300
I, well...

00:05:31.300 --> 00:05:32.970
Nyanperowna!

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:36.600
Hello. Please don't push.

00:05:44.230 --> 00:05:45.190
Come here.

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:51.240
Damn it!

00:05:54.910 --> 00:05:55.410
Huh?

00:05:56.990 --> 00:05:57.670
Nai!

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:00.040
Dammit...

00:06:05.710 --> 00:06:06.930
I-I-I am sorry!

00:06:07.540 --> 00:06:09.550
Nyanperowna, are you all right?

00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:10.420
Nyanta.

00:06:10.420 --> 00:06:11.510
Nyansuke.

00:06:25.650 --> 00:06:26.350
Gareki!

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:37.000
You... You wandered off by yourself, and got yourself chased!

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:45.160
<i>That man...</i>

00:06:45.160 --> 00:06:47.290
<i>He wasn't from the Security Forces...</i>

00:06:47.290 --> 00:06:49.140
<i>Why's he chasing Nai?</i>

00:06:49.140 --> 00:06:51.300
<i>In fact, who is he?</i>

00:06:52.920 --> 00:06:54.300
Let's go.

00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:29.580
Who is the closest to area N11 now?

00:07:30.210 --> 00:07:32.430
<i>Me... it's Yogi.</i>

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:34.960
Why are you in such a bad mood?

00:07:34.960 --> 00:07:38.890
<i>Wha– Please listen to me, Hirato-san!</i>

00:07:38.890 --> 00:07:42.940
<i>First, I was knocked down by this boy who came zipping through.</i>

00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:45.140
<i>Then, the people chasing after him stepped on my back so hard.</i>

00:07:45.140 --> 00:07:46.520
We've got information that the boy we met in the train is being chased.

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:49.270
After that, my head was even stepped on, and now it hurts...

00:07:49.940 --> 00:07:51.110
<i>We're going to protect him, aren't we?</i>

00:07:51.110 --> 00:07:52.450
<i>Please let me go.</i>

00:07:53.110 --> 00:07:54.990
<i>You are still in the middle of the performance.</i>

00:07:55.900 --> 00:07:58.400
<i>Make sure the townsfolk enjoy the show.</i>

00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:00.960
<i>Hello? Hey!</i>

00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:03.790
<i>Hey, are you listening to me, Hirato-san?</i>

00:08:11.960 --> 00:08:13.840
Hey, Gareki.

00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:14.720
What?

00:08:16.050 --> 00:08:18.980
If I go to the Circus, maybe Karoku...

00:08:19.550 --> 00:08:21.430
Not now.

00:08:21.430 --> 00:08:22.940
I have to find out who that man was–

00:08:25.430 --> 00:08:27.930
All right, I have incapacitated him.

00:08:27.930 --> 00:08:29.060
Gareki!

00:08:29.660 --> 00:08:31.060
Stop.

00:08:31.060 --> 00:08:32.690
Gareki... Gareki... Gareki.

00:08:32.690 --> 00:08:33.150
This brat is the one.
Gareki... Gareki... Gareki.

00:08:33.150 --> 00:08:34.440
Gareki... Gareki... Gareki.
This brat is the one.

00:08:34.440 --> 00:08:36.440
What? Then what should we do with this one?

00:08:36.440 --> 00:08:36.820
It'll be troublesome if we leave him here.

00:08:36.820 --> 00:08:37.990
<i>This is bad.
It'll be troublesome if we leave him here.</i>

00:08:37.990 --> 00:08:39.460
<i>I can't move...</i>

00:08:39.460 --> 00:08:40.660
Gareki!

00:08:41.160 --> 00:08:42.420
Kill him.

00:08:44.410 --> 00:08:45.790
<i>These guys...</i>

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:47.920
Gareki!

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:51.720
Hey! What are you guys doing?

00:08:51.720 --> 00:08:55.720
Using such a dangerous thing on an innocent boy...

00:08:56.670 --> 00:08:58.730
You're such bad guys.

00:08:58.730 --> 00:09:00.970
Who the hell are you?!

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:03.510
Eat this!

00:09:03.510 --> 00:09:05.520
<i>Candy Bar!</i>

00:09:09.230 --> 00:09:12.530
Why are you chasing these boys?

00:09:13.610 --> 00:09:18.040
In any case, I can't ignore such wicked deeds happening in front of me.

00:09:18.230 --> 00:09:20.610
Ba. Ba. Ba!

00:09:20.610 --> 00:09:23.920
Filled with the power of man's spirit!

00:09:24.210 --> 00:09:28.080
I'm the Sparkling Prince who makes your hearts throb!

00:09:35.460 --> 00:09:40.140
The Second Ship Fighter of the National Defense Organization, Circus, Yogi...

00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:41.640
is here!

00:09:42.300 --> 00:09:43.850
Circus...

00:09:44.390 --> 00:09:46.100
<i>Circus...</i>

00:09:50.560 --> 00:09:52.440
Come, I will be your opponent.

00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:53.730
Which one shall first...

00:09:53.730 --> 00:09:54.320
What?

00:09:56.520 --> 00:09:57.320
What the–?

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:06.780
Phew. What a relief.

00:10:06.780 --> 00:10:09.830
I get so nervous when I fight.

00:10:10.410 --> 00:10:13.340
Oh no, Nyanperowna got dirty.

00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:16.790
Hey, are you two okay?

00:10:17.750 --> 00:10:18.510
Good.

00:10:19.310 --> 00:10:24.060
Listen, I was told to bring you two along with me,

00:10:24.060 --> 00:10:26.930
so please follow me at once.

00:10:26.930 --> 00:10:29.390
W-Well, I want to ask you something.

00:10:29.390 --> 00:10:32.820
What? Can you wait for a moment?

00:10:33.390 --> 00:10:34.940
This is Yogi.

00:10:34.940 --> 00:10:35.900
Yes.

00:10:36.810 --> 00:10:39.070
Really, are you already up there?

00:10:40.070 --> 00:10:40.690
That was fast.

00:10:40.690 --> 00:10:42.280
<i>Circus was looking for us?
That was fast.</i>

00:10:42.280 --> 00:10:44.530
<i>Circus was looking for us?</i>

00:10:44.530 --> 00:10:46.460
<i>What does that mean?</i>

00:10:47.070 --> 00:10:49.240
Well, let's go.

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:57.210
Welcome to the Circus Ship!

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:13.570
I'm home!

00:11:13.570 --> 00:11:16.100
Welcome back. Welcome back.

00:11:16.100 --> 00:11:19.400
You two, answer, "I'm home."

00:11:19.400 --> 00:11:21.080
I'm home.

00:11:21.080 --> 00:11:23.110
Answer.

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:26.400
I’m home.

00:11:28.570 --> 00:11:31.590
Voice recognition registration is completed.

00:11:34.510 --> 00:11:38.510
I am happy to see you again, Gareki-kun, Nai-kun.

00:11:44.180 --> 00:11:46.050
Let me introduce myself again.

00:11:46.050 --> 00:11:51.190
I am Second Ship Captain of the National Defense Organization, Circus, Hirato.

00:11:52.100 --> 00:11:55.690
I am one of the members who are in charge of eliminating crimes from this world.

00:11:56.430 --> 00:12:00.690
Though actually, our specialty's to pursue special crimes.

00:12:00.690 --> 00:12:02.150
Regular crimes are under the jurisdiction of the Security Forces–

00:12:02.150 --> 00:12:02.950
Excuse me...
Regular crimes are under the jurisdiction of the Security Forces–

00:12:02.950 --> 00:12:05.820
Is Karoku here?

00:12:05.820 --> 00:12:11.330
I only found this, and there was this crimson liquid... I mean, blood...

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:14.990
Gareki told me we should ask Circus since this belongs to Circus.

00:12:14.990 --> 00:12:16.340
You've got it wrong.

00:12:22.210 --> 00:12:26.630
There is no one named Karoku among the members of Circus.

00:12:26.630 --> 00:12:30.550
That bracelet is certainly a Circus I.D.

00:12:30.550 --> 00:12:34.350
But it's an older model which should have been destroyed.

00:12:37.520 --> 00:12:43.610
Depending on your cooperation, we may be able
to find some clues about that person, Karoku.

00:12:44.280 --> 00:12:46.190
Yes, I will cooperate!

00:12:47.610 --> 00:12:49.280
By the way, Gareki-kun,

00:12:50.410 --> 00:12:52.290
you know a woman named Mine, don't you?

00:12:53.530 --> 00:12:54.790
No.

00:12:56.790 --> 00:12:59.800
I really find it adorable when I see young people acting tough.

00:13:00.710 --> 00:13:02.290
There's no need to be scared.

00:13:03.080 --> 00:13:04.170
Who are you calling scared–

00:13:04.170 --> 00:13:07.930
We found traces of blast marks at Mine's house.

00:13:07.930 --> 00:13:12.300
Your skill disposing of the bombs on the train was superb, too.

00:13:16.890 --> 00:13:19.930
Is it your way of showing consideration by choosing wealthy targets...

00:13:19.930 --> 00:13:22.070
who had gotten their riches through ill-gotten gains?

00:13:22.070 --> 00:13:26.770
I wonder why you need such a great amount of money.

00:13:30.820 --> 00:13:35.830
Oh sorry, I have no intention of persecuting you.

00:13:37.160 --> 00:13:42.000
When you were in contact with Mine, did her blood splash on you?

00:13:43.580 --> 00:13:45.840
What was that monster?

00:13:49.260 --> 00:13:50.180
"Varuga."

00:13:52.680 --> 00:13:58.140
We are after the criminal organization which has created those...

00:13:58.140 --> 00:14:01.440
awful monsters in the name of "Evolution."

00:14:09.730 --> 00:14:14.950
If their blood gets into your body, you will become like Mine.

00:14:16.780 --> 00:14:19.210
We will examine both of you.

00:14:20.330 --> 00:14:23.710
I regret to say you have no right to refuse.

00:14:23.710 --> 00:14:27.340
Woo, this is too serious.

00:14:27.340 --> 00:14:30.920
Why are you talking so authoritatively, Hirato-san?

00:14:30.920 --> 00:14:32.920
Oh, I didn't know you were here, Yogi.

00:14:32.920 --> 00:14:33.930
What?

00:14:35.300 --> 00:14:36.480
Oh, Gareki-kun,

00:14:37.760 --> 00:14:39.730
you did not kill Mine.

00:14:40.720 --> 00:14:42.020
Are you relieved?

00:14:43.640 --> 00:14:45.520
You don't like killing, do you?

00:14:52.610 --> 00:14:54.910
Circus got in your way?

00:14:56.200 --> 00:14:58.990
It's close to the town of Gavan.

00:14:58.990 --> 00:15:02.250
Sure, you can ask for "their" help.

00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:12.430
The blue flower blooms from blue seeds.

00:15:13.430 --> 00:15:18.350
But I am looking for red seeds.

00:15:22.430 --> 00:15:26.270
<i>The Second Ship Captain, Hirato.</i>

00:15:26.270 --> 00:15:28.450
<i>That young punk.</i>

00:15:32.110 --> 00:15:35.450
We will be heading to the town of Earthen Grounds, Gavan.

00:15:36.070 --> 00:15:39.960
I will leave Gareki and Nai's care to the two of you.

00:15:40.370 --> 00:15:41.530
Sure.

00:15:42.290 --> 00:15:44.750
Why us?

00:15:44.750 --> 00:15:48.340
Is it because you think we are not as good as the others?

00:15:48.340 --> 00:15:52.300
It's because I trust you.

00:15:52.300 --> 00:15:57.100
They've gotten away from Varuga, so there's a
possibility that they will become the enemy's target.

00:15:57.880 --> 00:15:59.730
Guarding someone is also an important assignment.

00:16:01.550 --> 00:16:03.980
Do you understand, Tsukumo?

00:16:06.140 --> 00:16:08.230
I'm sorry.

00:16:13.150 --> 00:16:15.650
Gareki, something was flying.

00:16:15.650 --> 00:16:16.740
What?

00:16:18.200 --> 00:16:21.500
Speaking of which, the ship has landed.

00:16:22.240 --> 00:16:23.620
Gareki?

00:16:26.160 --> 00:16:28.920
What? Gareki-kun, what are you doing?

00:16:28.920 --> 00:16:31.130
I'm going into town.

00:16:31.130 --> 00:16:34.590
What, what, what, no, no, no, no, no.

00:16:34.590 --> 00:16:35.960
It's so late.

00:16:35.960 --> 00:16:37.390
Let me go shopping.

00:16:37.390 --> 00:16:39.430
What? What are you buying?

00:16:39.430 --> 00:16:40.390
Things like clothes.

00:16:40.390 --> 00:16:41.550
Clothes? We have clothes. We have all sorts of clothes!

00:16:41.550 --> 00:16:43.760
Well, there is nothing to do.
Clothes? We have clothes. We have all sorts of clothes!

00:16:43.760 --> 00:16:44.650
It's boring.

00:16:44.650 --> 00:16:47.140
Well then, let's play hide and seek!

00:16:47.140 --> 00:16:49.900
What? How old are you?

00:16:49.900 --> 00:16:51.900
Well, I am 21 years old.

00:16:51.900 --> 00:16:53.900
But there are times when even adults want to play hide and seek!

00:16:56.400 --> 00:16:57.690
I will be "it".

00:16:57.690 --> 00:16:58.410
What?

00:16:59.610 --> 00:17:03.420
But ordinary people usually cannot keep up with me,

00:17:03.420 --> 00:17:05.910
so you don't have to play if you don't think you are up to the challenge.

00:17:08.370 --> 00:17:11.620
The time limit is one hour.

00:17:11.620 --> 00:17:16.930
One, two, three, four, five...

00:17:29.890 --> 00:17:30.690
That place is off-limits.

00:17:30.690 --> 00:17:31.480
Huh?
That place is off-limits.

00:17:31.480 --> 00:17:32.940
That place is off-limits.

00:17:39.190 --> 00:17:44.710
Off-limits. Off-limits. Off-limits. Off-limits...

00:17:44.710 --> 00:17:46.500
Off-limits.

00:17:50.250 --> 00:17:51.300
Yogi.

00:17:51.500 --> 00:17:53.470
Off-limits. Off-limits.

00:17:53.470 --> 00:17:56.960
Hey, stop, stop.
Off-limits. Off-limits.

00:17:56.960 --> 00:17:56.970
Hey, stop, stop.

00:17:58.090 --> 00:17:59.470
Hide and seek,

00:17:59.470 --> 00:18:01.970
somewhere where I can't be found.

00:18:21.030 --> 00:18:22.330
Whoa,

00:18:22.950 --> 00:18:26.080
I found red seeds.

00:18:32.410 --> 00:18:36.590
Since you came to me, why are you running away?

00:18:51.730 --> 00:18:56.110
Yogi, all victims seemed to have been deliberately killed.

00:18:56.770 --> 00:18:58.770
It's highly possible that this is a diversion.

00:18:58.770 --> 00:19:00.620
Strengthen the security around Gareki and Nai.

00:19:00.620 --> 00:19:01.950
It's too late!

00:19:12.010 --> 00:19:13.380
Tsukumo-chan!

00:19:27.340 --> 00:19:28.230
Oh no!

00:19:29.190 --> 00:19:30.510
Nai-chan, run away!

00:19:30.510 --> 00:19:31.820
Run, you dork!

00:19:33.850 --> 00:19:35.570
Run away as fast as you can!

00:19:38.200 --> 00:19:39.980
What are you doing?

00:19:39.980 --> 00:19:42.570
You're the main target, aren't you?!

00:19:42.570 --> 00:19:43.610
Gareki...

00:19:43.610 --> 00:19:44.690
Run!

00:19:48.030 --> 00:19:49.210
No way...

00:19:50.950 --> 00:19:51.710
Release...

00:19:52.580 --> 00:19:55.170
Release everyone!

00:20:00.500 --> 00:20:05.350
Our mission is to bring back the red seed.

00:20:05.840 --> 00:20:07.430
All right!

00:20:10.940 --> 00:20:14.440
She couldn't find you after one hour, right?

00:20:14.850 --> 00:20:15.310
Huh?

00:20:15.310 --> 00:20:17.730
Hide and seek is over.

00:20:43.630 --> 00:20:47.050
That Varuga was trying to take Nai-kun.

00:20:47.060 --> 00:20:50.180
Capture without killing, huh...

00:20:51.260 --> 00:20:52.810
That was scary, wasn't it?

00:20:52.810 --> 00:20:55.850
Let's take a warm bath.

00:20:55.850 --> 00:20:56.690
Bath...

00:21:07.110 --> 00:21:10.570
<i>Nai, Nai...</i>

00:21:10.570 --> 00:21:14.210
<i>I wonder if you can hear me well?</i>

00:21:14.210 --> 00:21:14.840
<i>Nai.</i>

00:21:19.870 --> 00:21:23.010
<i>Karoku, what are you doing?</i>

00:21:25.710 --> 00:21:26.800
I'm kissing.

00:21:30.470 --> 00:21:34.050
I heard you were involved in an incident, Erisyuka.

00:21:40.900 --> 00:21:42.810
Karoku!

00:21:45.690 --> 00:21:48.820
<i>Karoku, I've wanted to see you!</i>

00:21:48.820 --> 00:21:51.650
K-Karoku....

00:23:25.910 --> 00:23:26.540
Ah...

00:23:26.540 --> 00:23:27.490
What happened ~ma?

00:23:27.490 --> 00:23:30.290
Well, am I doing okay with Nyanperowna?

00:23:30.290 --> 00:23:31.500
It’s average ~ma.

00:23:31.500 --> 00:23:31.920
What?

00:23:31.920 --> 00:23:34.630
The sales of Nyanperowna merchandises haven't been changing ~ma.

00:23:34.630 --> 00:23:37.550
What? I am going to work harder to become popular!

00:23:37.550 --> 00:23:39.090
Try your best ~ma.
